    <div class="abstract-box">
      <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
      <p><em>Bacopa monnieri</em> is a perennial creeping herb extensively evaluated for verbal learning, memory consolidation, and free recall. Reviews of controlled human trials report promising findings in some memory measures after repeated use, with variation in extracts, populations, and outcomes. Acute findings are mixed: a small crossover trial reported improvements on selected tasks. These results do not establish a general cognitive-enhancement effect.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Evidence Matrix -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Synthesized Evidence Matrix</h2>
      <div class="evidenceStack">
        
        <div class="evidenceCard">
          <div class="evidence-type">
            <span class="evidence-area">Delayed Word Recall</span>
            <span class="evidenceTag">H1 · Systematic review</span>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-finding">
            A systematic review found some evidence for improved memory free recall across trials, generally lasting 12 weeks.
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-limitation">
            Small studies and differing extracts limit generalization. This summary does not establish a universal effect size or adverse-event rate.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="evidenceCard">
          <div class="evidence-type">
            <span class="evidence-area">Acute Reaction Time</span>
            <span class="evidenceTag">H2 · Controlled Trials</span>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-finding">
            A small acute crossover study reported improvement on selected cognitive tasks; results should not be generalized to all measures or products.
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-limitation">
            Limited sample size and extract-specific findings; the cited study does not establish a therapeutic steady-state explanation.
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

